---
import { blog, site } from '../data/portfolio';

/**
 * The rights and AI notice that closes the site.
 *
 * Worded carefully rather than boilerplate-ly, because the easy version would
 * be wrong. Copyright needs human authorship: text a model produced on its own
 * is not protected however firmly a footer asserts it. What Gianluca does own
 * is unambiguous — the artwork, the renders, the site itself, and the editorial
 * judgement of what gets published and how it is arranged — so the notice
 * claims that, separates it from the AI-assisted writing, and leaves other
 * people's press material to them.
 */
const year = new Date().getFullYear();
---

<section class="px-5 sm:px-8 md:px-10 pb-14">
  <div class="max-w-[880px] mx-auto rounded-[18px] border border-[#D7E2EA]/12 p-6 sm:p-8">
    <h2 class="text-[#D7E2EA]/45 font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-[0.64rem]">
      Rights, and how this site is made
    </h2>

    <div class="mt-5 space-y-4">
      <p class="text-[#D7E2EA]/65 font-light text-[0.86rem] leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-[#D7E2EA] font-medium">The artwork is mine.</strong> Every
        render, concept, environment and animation shown in the portfolio is my own
        work, © {year} {site.name}, all rights reserved. Nothing on these pages may be
        reproduced, used for training, or passed off as another studio's work without
        my written permission. The design and build of the site are mine too.
      </p>

      <p class="text-[#D7E2EA]/65 font-light text-[0.86rem] leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-[#D7E2EA] font-medium">Everything here is written
        and signed by me.</strong> I use research and drafting tooling the same
        way I use anything else in a pipeline, and nothing goes live until I have
        read it and approved it — there is no automatic publishing. What gets
        covered, what gets rejected, the angle, the corrections and the
        arrangement are mine, and so is the responsibility for them.
      </p>

      <p class="text-[#D7E2EA]/65 font-light text-[0.86rem] leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-[#D7E2EA] font-medium">It can still be wrong.</strong>
        Fast-moving coverage carries a real risk of small inaccuracies — a date,
        a figure, a name. I check what I can and articles link their sources. If
        something here matters to a decision you are making, verify it at the source.
        Spotted a mistake? <a href={`mailto:${blog.email}`} class="underline decoration-[#B600A8]/70 underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#D7E2EA] transition-colors">Tell me</a> and I will fix it.
      </p>

      <p class="text-[#D7E2EA]/65 font-light text-[0.86rem] leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-[#D7E2EA] font-medium">Other people's material.</strong>
        Screenshots, trailers and press images belong to their respective publishers
        and studios, and are used here for commentary and criticism, credited where
        they appear.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="text-[#D7E2EA]/30 font-light text-[0.74rem] leading-relaxed mt-6 pt-5 border-t border-[#D7E2EA]/10">
      More on the bylines and how the blog is written:
      <a href="/authors/" class="underline decoration-[#B600A8]/70 underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#D7E2EA]/60 transition-colors">who writes here</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
